What will you do?

As an Operator, you will work in a dynamic production environment within the fresh produce industry (potatoes, vegetables, and fruit). You will play an important role in the sorting process of avocados and mangoes, ensuring that production runs smoothly and efficiently.

During your first week, you will work on the sorting line to gain a thorough understanding of the production process. You will sort fruit based on its ripeness while learning how the sorting department operates. After this onboarding period, you will be paired with an experienced buddy who will guide and support you until you are confident enough to work independently.

Your responsibilities include:

- Working on the sorting line during your onboarding period, sorting fruit based on ripeness;
- Receiving and processing production orders using the computer;
- Translating production orders into clear instructions for the sorting team;
- Supervising a sorting line of approximately 7 employees;
- Monitoring the quality and progress of the production process.

This is a varied role in which you will combine hands-on production work with team leadership. You will continuously switch between planning, execution, and coordinating your team to ensure production targets are met.

Working Days & Hours

You will work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday, with occasional Saturdays when required.

Working hours: 06:45 AM – 03:30 PM, with occasional overtime until production has been completed.

- Available to work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday (occasional Saturdays);
- Comfortable working with computers;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Experience in the fresh produce industry is an advantage;
- Experience as an Operator or in a supervisory role;
- Able to lead and motivate a team;
- Stress-resistant and able to adapt to changing circumstances.

Technical| Duiven | Day shift | Aviation | Permanent position |

Are you technically minded and do you enjoy working with precision? Would you like to work with aviation safety equipment used by major international airlines? And are you looking for a long-term career with the possibility of a direct contract? Then this Technical Employee position in Duiven could be the perfect opportunity for you!

What are you going to do?
In this role, you will work with safety equipment used in commercial aircraft. Your job is to inspect, test and maintain critical aviation safety products according to strict technical manuals. You will always follow detailed English instructions and procedures. Precision and accuracy are extremely important, because the equipment you work with plays a vital role in passenger safety. You will work closely with colleagues from different departments and register your work in the internal system.

Your tasks include:

- Conducting inspections of aviation safety equipment, such as oxygen systems;
- Testing products by subjecting them to pressure tests and checking for leaks or defects;
- Carefully following detailed English technical manuals and safety procedures;
- Documenting inspections and results in the company system (Quantum);
- Communicating with colleagues from customer service and other departments;
- Identifying and reporting any irregularities immediately.

This is a full-time position (40 hours) from Monday to Friday, 07:00 – 16:00. In the future, the company may transition to a two-shift system, so flexibility is important.

What do we offer?
- Salary between €2,900 and €3,600 gross per month;
- You will start directly with the company, meaning you will be employed directly by the client from day one;
- Possibility of a permanent contract within a short time;
